# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock is deliberately committed. This crate is not a library — it
# compiles to a WASM binary that gets packaged into a .spkg and deployed, so the
# build must be reproducible. Without the lock, every image build re-resolved to
# "latest compatible" and a working build broke with no source change:
# substreams-antelope-core 0.7.0 was published, abigen picked it up while
# substreams-antelope stayed on 0.6.0, and the generated ABI bindings failed to
# compile against two versions of the same crate.

# Generated ABI bindings (regenerated by build.rs from abi/polaris.music.json)
src/abi/polaris_music.rs

# Substreams packages
*.spkg

# Output files
/output/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Substreams cache
.substreams/
